    thinking: "**Constructing Interactive Subcomponents**\n\nOkay, I\'m now focusing on building the interactive subcomponents, specifically `src/components/Navigation.tsx`. The goal is a glassmorphic header that transitions to solid on scroll. It will include the Toss logo, represented by stylized text and a custom blue ring icon. I\'m keen on achieving a sleek, modern aesthetic.\n\n\n**Designing App Download Modal**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in developing the interactive modal for app downloads, with a strong focus on a visually striking presentation. My current emphasis is on integrating a QR code for direct download access, accompanied by the option to simulate an SMS download link. I\'m aiming for a sophisticated, user-friendly interface. It\'s really neat!\n\n\n**Visualizing Score & Calculator**\n\nI\'m now diving into the development of two key interactive components. First, `CreditScoreSimulator.tsx`, will show a dynamic credit gauge with SVG stroke-dasharray animations, responding to checkboxes representing financial habits. Secondly, `FinancialCalculator.tsx` will let users simulate savings, using beautiful sliders for an engaging experience. I\'m focusing on user-friendly interactivity and visually appealing animations for both.\n\n\n**Developing Savings Simulator**\n\nI\'m now building the savings simulator, focusing on input fields for monthly savings (10k-5M KRW), period (1-5 years), and interest rate (1.5-8%). I\'m aiming for dynamic calculations that display principal, pre-tax interest, and after-tax payouts. A bar chart will visualize principal and interest growth. The final call to action is to find high-yield savings products.\n\n\n"
