    thinking: "**Designing the UI**\n\nI\'m starting to visualize the `CreditScoreSimulator` component, aiming for a UI that mirrors Toss\'s renowned \"\353\202\230\354\235\230 \354\213\240\354\232\251\354\240\220\354\210\230 \354\241\260\355\232\214 \353\260\217 \354\230\254\353\246\254\352\270\260\" service. I want to build a simulator that is intuitive and compelling. The goal is to capture the essence of Toss\'s service in a new and engaging manner.\n\n\n**Visualizing the Gauge**\n\nI am now focusing on the UI\'s left side. I am envisioning a dynamic, animated circular gauge using SVGs to display the credit score. The gauge will be centered around a baseline score of 720. Its color will change based on the credit score, transitioning from amber to Toss Blue and then to emerald green or a violet gradient. An animated indicator will show the user\'s percentile ranking. There will be subtext to track score boosts.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will now build the Credit Score Simulator component (`src/components/CreditScoreSimulator.tsx`). Toss revolutionized fintech in Korea with its \"My Credit Score\" checker. This component displays a custom SVG-based dynamic radial gauge, a real-time slider to track score adjustments, interactive card rows representing financial habits, and a mock integration with tax services requesting document approvals to animate score increments with micro-celebration animations."
